<Project>
  <!--
    Temporary NuGet audit suppression to unblock the release pipeline.

    Why this exists
    The project pins log4net 2.0.15, which has GHSA-4f7c-pmjv-c25w
    (moderate severity). All GitHub releases have been failing since
    2026-05-16 (build-27) because build/Build.csproj sets
    TreatWarningsAsErrors=true and NuGet audit (NU190x) is treated as
    an error.

    Why NuGetAudit and not WarningsNotAsErrors
    WarningsNotAsErrors only demotes compiler (csc) warnings. NU190x
    warnings are emitted by dotnet restore, not by the C# compiler,
    and are controlled by the NuGetAudit MSBuild property. Setting
    WarningsNotAsErrors=NU1902;1903;1904 in Directory.Build.props is
    silently ignored (verified by running the release pipeline).

    Remediation (TODO before this file can be deleted)
    1. Bump log4net 2.0.15 to a non-vulnerable version. The 2.0.x line
       appears abandoned; the latest is 3.3.2 as of 2026-07. log4net 3.x
       is a major-version jump with API changes (assembly loading,
       XmlConfigurator semantics) that needs a focused PR with QA.
    2. Audit other pinned packages for similar vulnerabilities.
    3. Re-enable NuGet audit (set NuGetAudit=true in this file or
       delete this file once restore produces no NU190x warnings).

    Until then, do not remove this file or the release pipeline will
    start failing again.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <NuGetAudit>false</NuGetAudit>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
